WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.750
This workbook's guidance splits the
work: inbound provisioning creates and

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.600
updates accounts, and Lifecycle Workflows
act on accounts that already exist.

3
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.350
It also sets three rules, and
the kit builds them in code.

4
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:17.988
One parameterized Logic App per
integration, not one per component.

5
00:00:17.988 --> 00:00:21.226
Block first: Disable user
account and Revoke all

6
00:00:21.226 --> 00:00:24.626
refresh tokens for user
run before the custom task.

7
00:00:24.626 --> 00:00:28.737
And custom tasks are idempotent,
and retry with a bound.

8
00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:31.088
Microsoft Learn sets the contract.

9
00:00:31.088 --> 00:00:36.289
Its page on the Lifecycle Workflows custom
task extension says that in launch and

10
00:00:36.289 --> 00:00:39.426
wait, the extension starts
the Logic App and waits;

11
00:00:39.426 --> 00:00:43.787
if no response arrives within the
wait, the task is considered failed.

12
00:00:43.787 --> 00:00:47.726
Learn's Graph reference sets the wait
at thirty minutes to three hours.

13
00:00:47.726 --> 00:00:50.235
The response is a POST to resume,

14
00:00:50.235 --> 00:00:55.063
with a status of completed or
failed, and Learn lists it in v1.0.

15
00:00:55.063 --> 00:01:00.753
And Learn's page on Microsoft Graph national
cloud deployments gives the clouds:

16
00:01:00.753 --> 00:01:05.424
GCC keeps the worldwide Graph, GCC
High and DoD have their own hosts,

17
00:01:05.424 --> 00:01:08.810
and a token for one cloud
doesn't work in another.
